  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following have same number of significant figures?<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00253</mn></math><br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0003</mn></math><br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />(D)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>163</mn></math><br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6rMo0",
      "text": "A, B and C only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0MoUh",
      "text": "C and D only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9Vvis",
      "text": "B and C only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GPQMR",
      "text": "A, C and D only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>All nonzero digits are significant. All zeros that are found between nonzero digits are significant.&nbsp;Leading zeros (to the left of the first nonzero digit) are not significant.&nbsp;Trailing zeros for a whole number that ends with a decimal point are significant.The number of significant figures of the given numbers are as follows:<br />Numbers&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;No. of significant figures<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00253</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> &nbsp;<br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0003</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math><br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math><br />(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>163</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>(A), (C) and (D) have the same number of significant figures.</p></blockquote>",
